{
  "description": "The cache list in APIDOCS.md shows one record whose rData has only value. ListCachedZones in DnsServerCore/WebServiceOtherZonesApi.cs (v15.5.0) writes cached records with WriteRecordsAsJson as records outside a zone: ttl as text with the time left, dnssecStatus and lastUsedOn always, nameIdn for internationalized names, and glueRecords, dnssecRecords, eDnsClientSubnet and responseMetadata when the cache holds them. NS records also get nameServerMetadata. The name server in responseMetadata is null when unknown. rData has the members WriteRecordAsJson writes for each record type outside a zone: the SOA intervals are text with their duration, the members only zone records have are left out, and flags and protocol are a string or a number depending on the record type, as in zones/record-data.patch.json. dataType and data hold negative answers, which the cache keeps too. zones lists the names of subzones as text, domainIdn is written for an internationalized domain, and domain, zones and records are always written. Confirmed with strict response validation against Technitium 15.5.0 containers on 2026-11-01: a second server holding a record of each type answered a conditional forwarder zone, and the cache was read after resolving each record and a name that does not exist.",
